CROSS-EXAMINATION TRANSCRIPT - KEY EXCERPTS

PW-1 (Eye-witness):

Q: You stated that the accused attacked the victim with a knife.
A: Yes.

Q: Did you see who started the fight?
A: The victim started shouting first.

Q: Did the victim attack the accused first?
A: I saw the victim push the accused.

Q: Was the accused carrying the knife before the fight started?
A: I did not see the knife initially.

Q: When did you see the knife?
A: When the accused took it out from his pocket.

Q: Did the accused aim at the victim's chest or vital organs?
A: No, he swung the knife wildly.

Q: How many times did the accused strike?
A: Only once or twice.

PW-2 (Eye-witness):

Q: You heard the altercation.
A: Yes, I heard shouting.

Q: Did you hear any threat to kill?
A: No, I did not hear any such threat.

Q: Did you see the injuries being caused?
A: I saw the victim bleeding.

Q: Were the injuries severe?
A: There was blood but the victim was walking.

Q: Did the victim go to the hospital immediately?
A: Yes, his friends took him.

DOCTOR (Medical Officer):

Q: You examined the victim on 21.04.2025.
A: Yes.

Q: What were the injuries?
A: Two incised wounds on the left arm, one on the shoulder.

Q: Were any vital organs affected?
A: No, only soft tissue injuries.

Q: Were the injuries life-threatening?
A: No, they were not life-threatening.

Q: What is your opinion about the weapon used?
A: Sharp-edged weapon, likely a knife.

Q: Could these injuries be caused in self-defence?
A: It is possible.